Some of these look like covers of the extremal rational semistable surfaces:
for example, 2xI9 6xI3 would be a triple cover of 4xI3 totally ramified at
two of the I3, and I18 I9 3xI2 3xI1 of I6I3I2I1, etc.  As we noticed
previously, I10I10 etc. gives 10.3.c.a.  From 4xI6 4xI3 we get 18.3.b.a,
from 2xI9 6xI3 we get 9.3.d.a, from I27 I3 6xI1 9.3.d.a, from 3xI9 I3I3 3xI1
9.3.d.a, and from I18 we get 18.3.b.a again.

